      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- SIS_SUBJECT_CODE\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\n- LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL\n- TIP_DETAIL\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n\n## Column Mapping\n- department: SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_CODE, SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- department code: SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- department name: SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- variance of the total number of units: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS\n- average number of enrolled students: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- enrollment category: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- library reserve material detail: LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR_KEY, LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG_KEY, LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.TERM_CODE, LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID, LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY\n- material status key: LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY\n- library course instructor key: LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR_KEY\n- library reserve catalog key: LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG_KEY\n- term code: LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.TERM_CODE\n- subject ID: LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID, TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n- tip material key: TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_KEY\n- tip material status key: TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY\n- tip ISBN: TIP_DETAIL.ISBN\n- subject title: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_TITLE\n- minimum tip material status key in a window: TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- responsible faculty name: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME\n- offer department name: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\n- degree-granting subjects: SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n- enrolled students: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- subjects offered by that department: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.OFFER_DEPT_CODE\n\n## Join Keys\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE <-> SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.COURSE_NUMBER\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE <-> SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.COURSE_NUMBER\n- LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID <-> TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID\n- TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID <-> TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For each department, what is the department name and the variance of the total number of units for subjects offered by that department, considering only subjects with more than 0 enrolled students and that are degree granting?\n```sql\nSELECT ssc.DEPARTMENT_CODE, ssc.DEPARTMENT_NAME, VARIANCE(sos.TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units_variance FROM SIS_SUBJECT_CODE ssc JOIN SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION scd ON ssc.COURSE_NUMBER = scd.COURSE JOIN SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY sos ON scd.COURSE = sos.COURSE_NUMBER WHERE sos.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0 AND scd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' GROUP BY ssc.DEPARTMENT_CODE, ssc.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY total_units_variance DESC;\n```\n2. For library reserve material details with material status key equal to 'U', show the library course instructor key, library reserve catalog key, term code, subject ID, the tip material key, tip material status key, tip ISBN, the subject title from the subject offered table, and the minimum tip material status key in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the number of enrolled students.\n```sql\nSELECT l.LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR_KEY, l.LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG_KEY, l.TERM_CODE, l.SUBJECT_ID, t.TIP_MATERIAL_KEY, t.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY, t.ISBN, s.SUBJECT_TITLE, MIN(t.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY) OVER (ORDER BY s.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS ROWS BETWEEN 3 PRECEDING AND 1 FOLLOWING) AS window_column FROM LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL l JOIN TIP_DETAIL t ON l.SUBJECT_ID = t.SUBJECT_ID JOIN TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED s ON t.SUBJECT_ID = s.SUBJECT_ID WHERE l.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY = 'U'\n```\n3. For each department, what is the department name, the variance of the total number of units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 enrolled students and that are degree granting), and the average number of enrolled students for those subjects? Also, classify each department as 'HIGH_ENROLLMENT' if its average enrolled students is at least 20% higher than the overall average, 'LOW_ENROLLMENT' if at least 20% lower, or 'AVERAGE' otherwise.\n```sql\nWITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT ssc.DEPARTMENT_CODE, ssc.DEPARTMENT_NAME, VARIANCE(sos.TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units_variance, AVG(sos.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS avg_enrolled_students FROM SIS_SUBJECT_CODE ssc JOIN SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION scd ON ssc.COURSE_NUMBER = scd.COURSE JOIN SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY sos ON scd.COURSE = sos.COURSE_NUMBER WHERE sos.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0 AND scd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' GROUP BY ssc.DEPARTMENT_CODE, ssc.DEPARTMENT_NAME ) SELECT inner_cte.DEPARTMENT_CODE, inner_cte.DEPARTMENT_NAME, inner_cte.total_units_variance, inner_cte.avg_enrolled_students, CASE WHEN inner_cte.avg_enrolled_students > overall.avg_all_enrolled * 1.2 THEN 'HIGH_ENROLLMENT' WHEN inner_cte.avg_enrolled_students < overall.avg_all_enrolled * 0.8 THEN 'LOW_ENROLLMENT' ELSE 'AVERAGE' END AS enrollment_category FROM inner_cte CROSS JOIN ( SELECT AVG(sos.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS avg_all_enrolled FROM SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION scd JOIN SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY sos ON scd.COURSE = sos.COURSE_NUMBER WHERE sos.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0 AND scd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' ) overall ORDER BY inner_cte.total_units_variance DESC;\n```\n4. For library reserve material details with material status key equal to 'U', show the library course instructor key, library reserve catalog key, term code, subject ID, the tip material key, tip material status key, tip ISBN, the subject title from the subject offered table, the minimum tip material status key in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the number of enrolled students, and also include the responsible faculty name and the offer department name from the subject offered table.\n```sql\nWITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT l.LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR_KEY, l.LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG_KEY, l.TERM_CODE, l.SUBJECT_ID, t.TIP_MATERIAL_KEY, t.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY, t.ISBN, s.SUBJECT_TITLE, MIN(t.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY) OVER ( ORDER BY s.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS ROWS BETWEEN 3 PRECEDING AND 1 FOLLOWING ) AS window_column, s.TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY FROM LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL l JOIN TIP_DETAIL t ON l.SUBJECT_ID = t.SUBJECT_ID JOIN TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED s ON t.SUBJECT_ID = s.SUBJECT_ID WHERE l.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY = 'U' ) SELECT inner_cte.LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR_KEY, inner_cte.LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG_KEY, inner_cte.TERM_CODE, inner_cte.SUBJECT_ID, inner_cte.TIP_MATERIAL_KEY, inner_cte.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY, inner_cte.ISBN, inner_cte.SUBJECT_TITLE, inner_cte.window_column, s.RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME, s.OFFER_DEPT_NAME FROM inner_cte JOIN TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED s ON inner_cte.TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY = s.TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor each department and each library reserve material detail with material status key equal to 'U' for subjects offered by that department, what are the department code, department name, the variance of the total number of units for degree-granting subjects with more than 0 enrolled students, the average number of enrolled students for those subjects, the enrollment category (classified as 'HIGH_ENROLLMENT' if the average enrolled students is at least 20% higher than the overall average, 'LOW_ENROLLMENT' if at least 20% lower, or 'AVERAGE' otherwise), the library course instructor key, library reserve catalog key, term code, subject ID, the tip material key, tip material status key, tip ISBN, the subject title, the minimum tip material status key in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the number of enrolled students, the responsible faculty name, and the offer department name from the subject offered table? Do not return any rounded answers."
