      "content": "The database connection is returning access-denied errors, so I cannot execute verification queries. I'll rely on the semantic network evidence and the documented precedent SQL patterns (which are fully retrieved) to construct the final query.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables (from Phase 1, all investigated via `semantic_get`):**\n\n- **SIS_SUBJECT_CODE** — subject code lookup mapping subject codes/course numbers to departments and schools. Key columns: `COURSE_NUMBER` (joins to `SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE`), `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`. Granularity: one row per subject code/course number.\n- **SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION** — course catalog descriptions with `COURSE` (joins to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.COURSE_NUMBER and SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.COURSE_NUMBER), `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` ('Y'/'N' flag). Granularity: one row per course description.\n- **SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY** — subject-level rollup per term with `TOTAL_UNITS`, `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`, `COURSE_NUMBER`, `OFFER_DEPT_CODE`/`OFFER_DEPT_NAME`. Granularity: one row per subject per term.\n- **LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL** — bridge table for reserve materials: `LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR_KEY`, `LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG_KEY`, `TERM_CODE`, `SUBJECT_ID`, `LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY` ('U' = Unknown per LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS lookup).\n- **TIP_DETAIL** — textbook program detail: `TIP_MATERIAL_KEY`, `TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY`, `ISBN`, `SUBJECT_ID`, `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY`.\n- **TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — textbook program subject offering: `SUBJECT_TITLE`, `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`, `RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME`, `OFFER_DEPT_NAME`, `OFFER_DEPT_CODE`, `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY` (PK).\n\n**Concepts / Column concepts investigated:** `concept_course_material_programs` (TIP + library reserve linked by SUBJECT_ID + TERM_CODE; never equate the two status-key domains), `concept_subject_offering_facts` (SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY carries both TOTAL_UNITS and NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS at subject grain), `column_concept_material_status_key`, `column_concept_subject_id`, `column_concept_enrollment_measures`, `column_concept_total_units` (decision guide: \"Unit statistics at subject-offering rollup level with offering department/school → use SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS\").\n\n**Metrics investigated:** `dw_3868` (exact structural precedent — department stats joined to status-'U' reserve materials with TIP details), `dw_4287` (status-'U' reserve + TIP window pattern), `dw_3311` (department unit-variance stats joined to status-'U' materials).\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n\n- Join keys confirmed by hints + column definitions: `SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE ↔ SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.COURSE_NUMBER`, `SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE ↔ SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.COURSE_NUMBER`, `LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID ↔ TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID`, `TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID ↔ TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID`, and `TIP_DETAIL.TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY ↔ TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY` (1:1, no fan-out).\n- `concept_course_material_programs` documents the parent-child chain TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED → TIP_DETAIL and LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED → LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences / Fitness\n\n- **Enrollment measure**: the question says \"enrolled students\" → `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` (per `column_concept_enrollment_measures` decision guide, subject-grain questions use SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS; the window ordering uses TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS per the hint decomposition and dw_3868/dw_4287 precedent). SUPPORTED.\n- **Total units**: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS is the only candidate carrying both units and enrollment at subject grain with a COURSE_NUMBER join to SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION (needed for IS_DEGREE_GRANTING). SUPPORTED.\n- **Department attribution**: department stats keyed by SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_CODE/DEPARTMENT_NAME; library side attributed via TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME. Precedent dw_3868 joins the two sides on `DEPARTMENT_NAME = OFFER_DEPT_NAME` — the same join applies here (\"for subjects offered by that department\").\n- **Window function**: `MIN(TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY) OVER (ORDER BY NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS ROWS BETWEEN 3 PRECEDING AND 1 FOLLOWING)` — identical to dw_3868/dw_4287/hint subqueries 2 & 4.\n\n### 4. Business Usage\n\ndw_3868 is the direct precedent: it computes a department-level aggregate CTE, a library-reserve/TIP detail CTE (with the same window), and joins them on department name = OFFER_DEPT_NAME. The current question replaces the Engineering-enrollment department CTE with the degree-granting units-variance/enrollment-category CTE from hint subqueries 1 & 3.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n\nAll Phase 1 entities investigated: 6 gold tables (`semantic_get`), 2 concepts + 4 column concepts (`semantic_get`), 3 precedent metrics (`semantic_get`). DB verification via `mysql_query` was attempted 4 times but the connection is refused (access denied), so verification is based on documented precedent SQL only.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\nCombine hint subquery 3 (department stats + enrollment category via CROSS JOIN overall average) with hint subquery 4 (status-'U' reserve materials + TIP details + window), joining on `DEPARTMENT_NAME = OFFER_DEPT_NAME` per dw_3868 precedent. SELECT exactly the 16 requested columns in the asked order.\n\n",
